{
    "background_story": "Capri was a brilliant mathematician with a passion for patterns and sequences. She spent most of her career studying the intricacies of enumeration, fascinated by the way numbers could be arranged and rearranged to reveal hidden truths. Her groundbreaking work on combinatorial enumeration led to the development of new algorithms and theorems, earning her international recognition. Capri's love for enumeration wasn't limited to her research; she also saw beauty in the everyday world. She would often take long walks, enumerating the different types of flowers, birds, and trees she encountered. Her unique perspective on the world inspired a new generation of mathematicians and scientists, showing them that even the most abstract concepts could be found in the beauty of nature.",
